IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`
IMPORT `je54-seat`
IMPORT `je54-seat-powers-and-penalties`

-- je54-tests-seat: one test at least for every exported question of the two seat modules.  The exports only pass their inputs on to the rule modules, whose own tests are elsewhere, so the point of these tests is the
-- wiring: an argument in the wrong place gives a wrong answer here.  Each case therefore uses values that differ from one another, and each day-sensitive export is tried on a day in the text of 1 January 2019 to
-- 27 September 2021 (1 June 2020) and on a day in the current text (28 October 2026), or on the edge of the Article.  Expected values were written from the text of the Articles before this module was run.

`V1 day` MEANS YMD 2020 6 1
`V2f day` MEANS YMD 2026 10 28
`before 2019` MEANS YMD 2018 12 31

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading a` MEANS `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading b` MEANS `the day the enactment was passed or made`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`an instant in UTC` y mo d h mi s MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD y mo d) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mi s) "Etc/UTC"

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Local moment`
`the local moment` y mo d h mi s MEANS
    `Local moment` WITH
        `calendar day` IS YMD y mo d
        `hour of the day` IS h
        `minute of the hour` IS mi
        `second of the minute` IS s

GIVEN named IS A DATE
      made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that names the day` named `and was made on` made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `on a particular day`
        `the day it names` IS JUST named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

`the April enactment` MEANS `an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `and was made on` (YMD 2020 3 1)
`the later enactment` MEANS `an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `and was made on` (YMD 2024 2 1)

§ `The text, and Article 1`

#ASSERT `which text of the Law was in force on a day` `V1 day` EQUALS `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021`
#ASSERT `which text of the Law was in force on a day` `V2f day` EQUALS `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current`
#ASSERT `which text of the Law was in force on a day` `before 2019` EQUALS `the inferred text from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018`
#ASSERT `which text of the Law was in force on a day` (YMD 1900 1 1) EQUALS `no text before 28 March 2003`

#ASSERT (`on what day did the enactment come into force` `the April enactment` `reading a`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2020 4 1
#ASSERT (`on what day did the enactment come into force` `the April enactment` `reading b`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
#ASSERT REFUSED `on what day did the enactment come into force` `the later enactment` `reading a`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

#ASSERT DATETIME_SERIAL ((`at what moment did the enactment come into force` `the April enactment` "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the moment`) EQUALS DATETIME_SERIAL (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 23 0 0)
#ASSERT (`was the enactment in force on a day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `the April enactment` `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT NOT (`was the enactment in force on a day` (YMD 2020 3 31) `the April enactment` `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`was the enactment in force at a moment` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 23 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" `the April enactment` `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT NOT (`was the enactment in force at a moment` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 22 59 59) "Europe/Jersey" `the April enactment` `reading a`)'s `the answer`

#ASSERT `is the instrument an enactment` `V1 day` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is the instrument an enactment` `V2f day` `something that is none of these` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `is the instrument an enactment` `before 2019` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` `V1 day` (YMD 2020 5 10) (YMD 2020 5 20) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 5 20
#ASSERT `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` `V1 day` (YMD 2020 5 25) (YMD 2020 5 20) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 5 25
#ASSERT REFUSED `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` `V2f day` (YMD 2020 5 10) (YMD 2020 5 20) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 1(2) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not among the provisions answered before 1 January 2019"
#ASSERT `how is a reference to passing or repeal read` `V1 day` `repeal` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the rescission of the enactment`
#ASSERT `how is a reference to passing or repeal read` `V2f day` `passing` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the making of the enactment`
#ASSERT `how is a reference to passing or repeal read` `V2f day` `passing` FALSE EQUALS `as written`
#ASSERT `which date of promulgation is to be used` TRUE (JUST (YMD 2019 12 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2019 12 1
#ASSERT `which date of promulgation is to be used` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 1 1

§ `Articles 2, 3, 4, 5 and the Schedule`

#ASSERT `how is the word of the enactment read` `V1 day` `a word importing the masculine gender` FALSE EQUALS `the word includes females`
#ASSERT `how is the word of the enactment read` `V2f day` `a word in the plural` FALSE EQUALS `the word includes the singular`
#ASSERT REFUSED `how is the word of the enactment read` `before 2019` `a word in the plural` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT `does person include this body` `V1 day` `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE `the proviso limits Article 3 only` EQUALS `by Article 3 and by the Schedule`
#ASSERT `does person include this body` `V2f day` `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1950 6 1) FALSE `the proviso limits Article 3 only` EQUALS `by the Schedule only`
#ASSERT `does person include this body` `V2f day` `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1950 6 1) FALSE `the proviso also limits the Schedule definition of person` EQUALS `not at all`
#ASSERT `what does the Schedule definition do for the word` "advocate" `V1 day` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `within the word, as the Schedule says`
#ASSERT `what does the Schedule definition do for the word` "advocate" `V2f day` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `outside the word, because the Schedule says means`
#ASSERT `what does the Schedule definition do for the word` "land" `V1 day` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers` EQUALS `not named by the Schedule, which says includes and so does not shut it out: the word's own meaning decides`
#ASSERT (`was the thing done by midnight on the day` (YMD 2020 6 10) (`the local moment` 2020 6 10 23 59 59))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT NOT (`was the thing done by midnight on the day` (YMD 2020 6 10) (`the local moment` 2020 6 11 0 0 0))'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`was the thing done by midnight on the day` (YMD 2020 6 10) (`the local moment` 2020 6 10 23 59 59))'s `the basis` EQUALS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
#ASSERT (`was the thing done by midnight on the day` (YMD 2010 6 30) (`the local moment` 2010 6 30 12 0 0))'s `the basis` EQUALS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
#ASSERT `what does the commonly used name mean` `V1 day` "the Bailiff's Chambers" FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff's Chambers"
#ASSERT REFUSED `what does the commonly used name mean` `V2f day` "the Royal Court House" TRUE

§ `Article 7: service by post`

GIVEN authorized IS A BOOLEAN
      addressed IS A BOOLEAN
      prepaid IS A BOOLEAN
      posted IS A BOOLEAN
      delivery IS A `Local moment`
      proved IS A MAYBE `Local moment`
GIVETH A `Service by post as it happened`
`a letter` authorized addressed prepaid posted delivery proved MEANS
    `Service by post as it happened` WITH
        `the enactment authorizes or requires the document to be served by post` IS authorized
        `the letter was properly addressed` IS addressed
        `the letter was prepaid` IS prepaid
        `the letter was posted` IS posted
        `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS delivery
        `the other time proved` IS proved

`the Friday letter` MEANS `a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the local moment` 2024 3 4 9 0 0) NOTHING
`the Friday letter, a different time proved` MEANS `a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the local moment` 2024 3 4 9 0 0) (JUST (`the local moment` 2024 3 2 14 5 0))
`the Friday letter, unstamped` MEANS `a letter` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the local moment` 2024 3 4 9 0 0) NOTHING

#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2024 3 1) `the Friday letter` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2024 3 1) `the Friday letter, unstamped` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2024 3 1) `the Friday letter` TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 7 does not say when or whether service by post is then deemed effected"
#ASSERT (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2024 3 1) `the Friday letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2024 3 1) `the Friday letter, a different time proved` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 2
#ASSERT `on what day is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2024 3 1) `the Friday letter` FALSE `the time that is proved` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT REFUSED `on what day is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2024 3 1) `the Friday letter, a different time proved` FALSE `the Article gives no time`
        BECAUSE "the contrary is proved: on the reading that Article 7 says nothing of the time once the presumption is rebutted, the Article gives no time"
#ASSERT REFUSED `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2018 12 31) `the Friday letter` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 8: bankruptcy`

`a company` MEANS
    `Person who may have become bankrupt` WITH
        `is a company` IS TRUE
        `is a limited liability company` IS FALSE
        `is a bank` IS FALSE
`a limited liability company` MEANS
    `Person who may have become bankrupt` WITH
        `is a company` IS FALSE
        `is a limited liability company` IS TRUE
        `is a bank` IS FALSE



`the limited liability company winding up` MEANS `a limited liability company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022`
`the administration order` MEANS `an administration order is made in respect of a company under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`

-- A winding up of a limited liability company on 31 August 2022 (the day before the limb was inserted): not a person becoming bankrupt on the day of the event, and one on the day the question is asked.
#ASSERT NOT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `the limited liability company winding up` `a limited liability company` (YMD 2022 8 31) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `the limited liability company winding up` `a limited liability company` (YMD 2022 8 31) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
#ASSERT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `the limited liability company winding up` `a limited liability company` (YMD 2022 9 1) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `the administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 6 19) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT NOT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `the administration order` `a company` (YMD 2026 6 18) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
#ASSERT REFUSED `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `the administration order` `a company` (YMD 2018 12 31) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Articles 9 and 10`

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of division referred to`
      number IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Reference by number or letter`
`a reference in the Sample Law to` kind number MEANS
    `Reference by number or letter` WITH
        `the kind of division named` IS kind
        `the number or letter given` IS number
        `further identification is given` IS FALSE
        `the kind of instrument that contains the reference` IS `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council`
        `the instrument that contains the reference` IS "the Sample (Jersey) Law 2020"
        `the division that contains the reference` IS "Article 5"

#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` `V1 day` (`a reference in the Sample Law to` `a Schedule` "1"))'s `the place it is in` EQUALS "the Sample (Jersey) Law 2020"
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` `V2f day` (`a reference in the Sample Law to` `a sub-clause` "(b)"))'s `the place it is in` EQUALS "Article 5"
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` `V2f day` (`a reference in the Sample Law to` `a sub-clause` "(b)"))'s `the number or letter` EQUALS "(b)"
#ASSERT `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` `V1 day` `the enactment as amended` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` `V1 day` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 9(3) as it read before 28 September 2021 says amended from time to time and does not say revised or otherwise consolidated"
#ASSERT `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` `V2f day` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
#ASSERT `does Article 9 apply to the instrument` `V2f day` `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` (YMD 1954 8 21) EQUALS `as it stands, the instrument being a Law`
#ASSERT `does Article 9 apply to the instrument` `V1 day` `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` (YMD 1900 1 1) EQUALS `with the necessary changes, the instrument being a subordinate enactment`
-- Article 10: the other enactment passed on 22 August 1954 is after the commencement of the Law; on 20 August 1954 it is not; on 21 August 1954 the Law gives no time of day.
#ASSERT `do the expressions in the other enactment have the same meaning as in the enabling enactment` `V2f day` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `do the expressions in the other enactment have the same meaning as in the enabling enactment` `V1 day` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `do the expressions in the other enactment have the same meaning as in the enabling enactment` `V1 day` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 21) FALSE
        BECAUSE "the Law gives no time of day for its own commencement on 21 August 1954, so Article 10 cannot say whether an enactment passed that day was passed after it"

§ `Articles 11 and 11A`

`no circumstances` MEANS
    `Circumstances of an office` WITH
        `the office is vacant` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office has been removed or suspended from office` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office is absent temporarily or permanently` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office is incapacitated in a way that affects the person's performance` IS FALSE
`an absent holder` MEANS
    `Circumstances of an office` WITH
        `the office is vacant` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office has been removed or suspended from office` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office is absent temporarily or permanently` IS TRUE
        `the person holding the office is incapacitated in a way that affects the person's performance` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `may the power be exercised or the duty performed on this occasion` `V1 day` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may the power be exercised or the duty performed on this occasion` `V2f day` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `V1 day` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `V2f day` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
#ASSERT `does the power to pass an enactment include the power to repeal or amend it` `V1 day` TRUE `to repeal it` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `does the power to pass an enactment include the power to repeal or amend it` `V1 day` TRUE `some other act on it` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `does the power to pass an enactment include the power to repeal or amend it` `V2f day` TRUE `to repeal it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT `may the power to make an enactment be exercised in this way` `V1 day` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make any lesser provision, whether by way of exception or otherwise` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may the power to make an enactment be exercised in this way` `V1 day` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 28) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `may the power to make an enactment be exercised in this way` `V2f day` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in some other way` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` `V2f day` TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` `an absent holder` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` `V2f day` TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` `no circumstances` FALSE
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` `V2f day` TRUE `to remove or suspend a person from the office` `no circumstances` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` `V1 day` TRUE `to remove or suspend a person from the office` `no circumstances` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11A of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is inserted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"

§ `Articles 12 and 13`

GIVEN names IS A LIST OF STRING
      customary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Offences arising from one act or omission`
`offences under` names `and the customary law` customary MEANS
    `Offences arising from one act or omission` WITH
        `the enactments that create the offences` IS names
        `it is also an offence under the customary law of Jersey` IS customary

`the Alpha and Beta offences` MEANS `offences under` (LIST "the Alpha (Jersey) Law 2020", "the Beta (Jersey) Law 2021") `and the customary law` FALSE

#ASSERT `may the offender be prosecuted and punished under this enactment` `V1 day` `the Alpha and Beta offences` "the Beta (Jersey) Law 2021" FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may the offender be prosecuted and punished under this enactment` `V2f day` `the Alpha and Beta offences` "the customary law of Jersey" FALSE
#ASSERT `is the offender liable to be punished again for the same offence` `V1 day` `the Alpha and Beta offences` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is the offender liable to be punished again for the same offence` `V2f day` `the Alpha and Beta offences` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `is the offence punishable by the penalty proposed` `V1 day` TRUE 5 5 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is the offence punishable by the penalty proposed` `V2f day` TRUE 5 6 FALSE
#ASSERT `is the fine of an unlimited amount` `V1 day` TRUE `neither an amount nor a level on the standard scale is specified`
#ASSERT NOT `is the fine of an unlimited amount` `V2f day` TRUE `a level on the standard scale is specified`
#ASSERT `may the penalties be imposed alternatively or cumulatively` `V1 day` TRUE `cumulatively` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `may the penalties be imposed alternatively or cumulatively` `V2f day` FALSE `cumulatively` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 13(3) deals only where, in an enactment, more than one penalty is specified for an offence and the word and is used; it says nothing of the word or or of any other way of joining penalties"

§ `Articles 14 and 15`

#ASSERT `does the deviation from the prescribed form invalidate the form used` `V1 day` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the deviation does not invalidate the form used`
#ASSERT `does the deviation from the prescribed form invalidate the form used` `V2f day` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Article 14 does not save the form used, and does not say that it is invalid`
#ASSERT `was the distance measured the way the Law requires` `V1 day` (`Distance as measured` WITH `the distance` IS 100, `the unit` IS "metres", `the way it was measured` IS `in a straight line on a horizontal plane`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `was the distance measured the way the Law requires` `V2f day` (`Distance as measured` WITH `the distance` IS 100, `the unit` IS "metres", `the way it was measured` IS `in another way`) FALSE

§ `Articles 6, 16 and 17 (the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 only)`

#ASSERT `is the repeal of a repealing enactment barred from reviving the earlier enactment` `V1 day` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is the repeal of a repealing enactment barred from reviving the earlier enactment` `V1 day` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `is the repeal of a repealing enactment barred from reviving the earlier enactment` `V2f day` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 6 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT `do the repealed provisions remain in force at the instant` `V1 day` TRUE (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 23 59 59) (JUST (`an instant in UTC` 2020 4 1 0 0 0))
#ASSERT NOT `do the repealed provisions remain in force at the instant` `V1 day` TRUE (`an instant in UTC` 2020 4 1 0 0 0) (JUST (`an instant in UTC` 2020 4 1 0 0 0))
#ASSERT `does the repeal of an amended enactment include the repeal of its amendments` `V1 day` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `does the repeal of an amended enactment include the repeal of its amendments` `V1 day` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `may the power be exercised before the Law comes into force` `V1 day` `a Law passed after the commencement of the Law` (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2020 6 2) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may the power be exercised before the Law comes into force` `V1 day` `Regulations passed by the States` (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2020 5 31) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `may the enactment passed under the power come into force at the instant` `V1 day` `Regulations passed by the States` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 9 1 0 0 0) (`an instant in UTC` 2020 9 1 0 0 0) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may the enactment passed under the power come into force at the instant` `V1 day` `Regulations passed by the States` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 8 31 23 59 59) (`an instant in UTC` 2020 9 1 0 0 0) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `is a reference to the provisions repealed a reference to the provisions re-enacted` `V1 day` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `is a reference to the provisions repealed a reference to the provisions re-enacted` `V2f day` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 17 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT `does the repeal leave what was done, acquired, incurred or begun untouched` `V1 day` TRUE `affecting any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment repealed` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `does the repeal leave what was done, acquired, incurred or begun untouched` `V1 day` TRUE `some other effect` FALSE
#ASSERT `may the proceeding be brought or the penalty imposed as if the repealing enactment had not been passed` `V1 day` TRUE `imposing a penalty, forfeiture or punishment` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `may the proceeding be brought or the penalty imposed as if the repealing enactment had not been passed` `V1 day` TRUE `something else` FALSE
#ASSERT `does paragraph 2 apply to the enactment that ceased` `V1 day` `the enactment expired`
#ASSERT NOT `does paragraph 2 apply to the enactment that ceased` `V1 day` `the enactment ceased in some other way`

§ `The years before 2019 for the second seat module`

#ASSERT REFUSED `may the penalties be imposed alternatively or cumulatively` `before 2019` TRUE `cumulatively` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
